                <pb facs="0492" n="484" sameAs="frus:frus1939v02/pg484"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">851.012/101: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in France</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Bullitt</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Paris</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1939-10-27T17:00:00+01:00">October 27, 1939—5
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received October 27—3:58 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2597. My 3853 of February 16, 1939<anchor n="8" xml:id="d431-f1"/> transmitting
                    copy and translation French Nationality Law of August 10, 1927 as modified by
                    the decree of November 12, 1938 Articles 2 and 4 of the law of August 10, 1927
                    are replaced for the duration of hostilities by a decree dated October 19, 1939
                    and effective October 27, 1939 providing that renunciation of French nationality
                    must be made by individuals of the masculine sex within 3 months after arrival
                    at the age of 18 years and that failure to renounce French nationality within
                    the prescribed period will render the persons concerned subject to military
                    service in the class of their age. Those individuals who have passed 18 years of
                    age and are less than 22 years of age are permitted to renounce French
                    nationality within the 3 months following the publication of the decree on
                    October 27, 1939.</p>
                <p>Full report by mail.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Bullitt</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
